# Rule: Brandmark / sigil choreography

Edits here move a brandmark actor across fixed, projected, or in-canvas renderers. Small measurement mistakes show up as hero flashes, between-section float, practice snaps, or a visible SVG-to-particle size jump.

**Read first:** `sentinel/decisions/010-brandmark-choreography.md`, `sentinel/decisions/023-corridor-brandmark-physics-core.md`, `.claude/skills/brandmark-choreography/SKILL.md`, `sentinel/decisions/008-landing-v7-background-layers.md`.

**Process:** `sentinel/MAINTENANCE.md` - live rects, `onLeave` settlement; avoid CSS sticky hacks without an ADR.

**Home-v2 corridor invariant:** the live corridor brandmark is a **single particle painter**. `BrandmarkPhysicsCoreActor` owns the visible mark end-to-end; `ProjectedBrandmarkActor` stays mounted only as a structural/world-anchor helper and its DOM SVG remains hidden. Current model (async-flow morph, 2026-06-24): the flat rest mark is already a dense particle silhouette (`coverMorphRef = 1`, `uDepth = 0`, full draw density, larger flat dots). As `uDepth` rises, the vertex shader gives each particle a deterministic stagger from seed + polar position, offsets it along a small tangent/asymmetric XY arc, pulls it backward on local Z at the flow midpoint, then settles it onto its sampled domed home inside the sphere. Density relaxes with depth (`depthKeep`) from a near-solid 2D particle mark to the calmer in-sphere corridor budget. `uStream` / `uGlitch` are gated from depth so they join the particle flow after it begins. Pitfalls: reintroducing visible DOM SVG, SVG opacity fade, z-index handoff, `coverMorph` 0→1 as the primary transition, a separate `reveal` opacity multiplier on the core, uniform `pos.z *= uDepth` slab motion, or lowering `ignite` to create a swirl. The sim must remain assembled (`seedAtHome`, `ignite=1`); the render shader owns the asynchronous flow.

**One ring on the rig; cases are a DOM overlay (ADR-029 + ADR-035, supersedes the ADR-033 orbit + ADR-034 terrace):** `pointerLookRef` carries ONLY the services card ring (`ServicesCardRing`, scroll-owned via the runway progress ref). There is NO in-canvas cases object and NO camera channel for the cases. The four Build-park cases render in `ArcCasesTerminal` — a fixed DOM overlay in `HomeCorridor` (chip under the Build title), CLICK-owned (`arcCasesStore` + a damped arm level; scroll only gates via `arcBandFactor`), unfurled by a CSS clip-path transition. The corridor camera is a pure Z dolly (the ADR-034 `arcCameraShiftX` / `getTerraceViewportLayout` / terrain shroud are RETIRED). The only touchpoint here is `gateStackLabel` (sceneGeom): while armed the sources/surfaces DOM labels fade on `arcCasesLevelRef` (single writer = the overlay's DOM rAF, NOT a useFrame; unarmed / flag-off = literal 1). Cases and services-ring windows are provably disjoint (cases dead by epilogue 0.1; services entrance needs dissipate >= 0.6 which needs epilogue >= 0.72) — never weaken either clock. No wall-clock motion (ADR-021); gate parity `ARC_CASES_MEDIA` == the CSS hide of the chip dock + overlay. Do not re-introduce an in-canvas cases ring/slab, a camera channel, or an ADR-032-style drawer.
